{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only experiments clearly establish that scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the best RNA configuration (config_006: 0.653 acc, transformer aggregation; config_005: 0.650, avgpool). The image modality is unexplored beyond a weak resnet50 baseline (config_010: 0.208 acc). The biggest remaining design uncertainty is whether adding image features via fusion can complement the strong RNA signal or will only add noise. This experiment (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) directly tests that question by pairing the best RNA setup with a stronger image encoder (ViT-L vs. the weak ResNet50) and a simple concat fusion. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it resolves the highest-impact unknown—whether multimodal fusion adds value at all—before committing further experiments to the multimodal space; (2) it uses a direct comparison to config_006 (same RNA encoder, profile, and aggregation) so the effect of adding image is isolated; (3) choosing ViT-L over ResNet50 avoids confounding a negative result with a known-weak image encoder, making the outcome more interpretable; and (4) the result will inform whether to invest remaining budget in tuning fusion strategy, image encoder, or aggregation in the multimodal setting."
}

